@@ -0,0 +1,264 @@
+# DTI-00B offline meter prototype 0.1.0
+
+Research only, baseline `c8d8d620dfed06caee92a498b891bf2faa37a6a9` /
+`be3470c378180aa215d527c6de6b686583ae0d79`. No app imports, third-party
+dependencies, service, database, Auth, Visit writes, Fingerprint changes or
+production activation. Offline commands never access a capture interface;
+R2 adds an explicitly selected Linux research live adapter (below). This is not DTI-01 and does not
+declare DTI-00 accepted. Suricata counters are never an accounting fallback.
+
+## Input and native basis
+
+Local classic PCAP v2.4, Ethernet link type 1, either byte order, microseconds or
+nanoseconds. Ordered timestamps are mandatory; malformed framing aborts the
+attempt. One explicit synthetic subject MAC/site scope per manifest. At most
+two VLAN tags. Unicast IPv4/IPv6 only; broadcast, multicast, ARP, other L2 and
+subject-to-itself frames are outside accounting. IPv6 base Next Header is exposed;
+extension-chain interpretation and jumbograms are not supported. Zero IPv6 payload
+length is conservatively rejected (including valid empty IPv6): **degraded**, not
+a healthy zero. These limitations are prototype-only, not a final scope freeze.
+
+IPv4 bytes are total_length; IPv6 bytes are 40 + payload_length. Captured length,
+Ethernet length and application bytes are not the metric. Header-only snaplen is
+accepted when complete L2/IP headers and original wire length corroborate the IP
+length. Known bad/truncated headers degrade their interval. Structural PCAP errors,
+unsorted timestamps and hard limits block the overall attempt, even if earlier
+rows were emitted. Never ingest a partial output as a COMPLETE replay.
+
+Reader retains at most 82 Ethernet/IP header bytes per packet and discards remaining
+record bytes in <=4096-byte blocks without interpreting/retaining payload. Generated
+fixtures contain Ethernet/IP headers only, with declared wire lengths; no actual
+visitor captures, TCP/application data or arbitrary visitor history are generated.
+PCAPNG is intentionally unsupported.
+
+Format references: [classic PCAP draft](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-opsawg-pcap-05.html)
+(descriptive draft, not a production standard freeze),
+[IPv4 RFC 791](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc791),
+[IPv6 RFC 8200](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8200).
+
+## Coverage and output
+
+Closed `coverage.json`: capture_source_id, test_scope, subject_mac,
+coverage_start_utc, coverage_end_utc, capture_quality_intervals. Each interval has
+start_utc/end_utc/state and the ordered intervals exactly partition coverage.
+States: healthy, partial, degraded, source_unavailable, prototype_unavailable.
+Optional synthetic_visit_boundary_utc and synthetic_duplicate_records are
+research fixture metadata, NOT final production fields. Source/site identities
+are explicitly supplied, never guessed from IP addresses. Canonical UTC times
+are represented with nine fractional digits, so nanoseconds do not round across
+half-open boundaries.
+
+Default slices are UTC epoch-aligned [start,end), 5 seconds. Partial coverage edges
+are incomplete, not zeros. Optional Visit T divides a bucket into two declared
+experimental subintervals, conserving counts; normal cadence remains 5 seconds.
+`stop_at` in the Python API simulates restart: the open bucket is partial, later
+buckets prototype_unavailable; a new Coverage/run UUID resumes separately.
+Sequence resets per run; durable restart/ingest policy is not implemented.
+
+Every JSONL slice contains schema_version=1, prototype_version=0.1.0,
+capture_source_id, test_scope, subject_key, slice_start_utc, slice_end_utc,
+slice_id, run_session_id, source_sequence, upload_packets, download_packets,
+upload_bytes_native, download_bytes_native, first_packet_at, last_packet_at,
+capture_quality_state, quality_reasons, complete_accounting,
+upload_bytes_per_second, download_bytes_per_second,
+healthy_absence_of_subject_traffic. No raw IP/header/payload is emitted.
+
+Counts in incomplete intervals mean **observed lower-bound counts**, not complete
+traffic totals. Rates are null unless healthy. Healthy zero needs proven coverage;
+missing/degraded capture and prototype gaps never assert idle. Slice end/packet
+times permit future activity/freshness decisions, without freezing product policy.
+Rate is emitted when a bucket completes, not when its flow terminates.
+
+slice_id is SHA256 of canonical semantic identity: schema/source/scope/subject/
+start/end. Semantic accounting payload excludes run UUID/sequence. Repeated bounded
+input gives REPLAY even with a new UUID; same slice ID with changed accounting or
+quality is CONFLICT, never a second valid increment. Output ingestion is future scope.
+
+## Duplicates: explicit limitation, not a production PASS
+
+Raw native counters count all observed in-scope records before dedup. No TCP
+sequence/header/timestamp similarity heuristic suppresses packets. Real retransmission
+is counted, even with identical IP headers. Without explicit provenance every record
+counts, including a potential mirrored repeat. Classic PCAP headers alone cannot
+prove mirror origin rather than a legitimate second transmission.
+
+The exact synthetic duplicate fixture declares repeated ordinal -> original ordinal
+in synthetic_duplicate_records. This is a trusted independent generator assertion of
+**one original transmission**, not inferred by the meter. It is corroborated by equal
+bounded headers/native length and a retained original within the configured horizon.
+Default horizon 1 second, cache max 4096 entries (both configurable downward).
+Eviction/expired/nonmatching provenance retains the packet and degrades quality.
+The full payload is deliberately not hashed/required; equal headers cannot establish
+full-frame equality. Thus the assertion must come from trusted synthetic provenance.
+Untrusted/ordinary real PCAP cannot use this assertion as production dedup authority.
+
+False positive risk: a wrong provenance assertion could suppress a real transmission
+with equal headers. False negative risk: without provenance, or beyond the horizon/
+cache bound, duplicates remain counted. Provenance uncertainty is never hidden as
+healthy dedup. Counters include raw_packets_seen, raw_packets_in_scope,
+raw_bytes_native, accounted_packets/bytes, duplicate_candidates,
+deduplicated_packets, dedup_cache_entries/peak/evictions,
+duplicate_provenance_unresolved, rejected/out-of-scope/outside-coverage records.
+**General mirror-duplicate admission remains PARTIAL (G26 unresolved).** Do not claim
+the complete DTI-00B admission PASS based only on the synthetic case.
+
+## Resource bounds and degradation candidate
+
+One subject, one current bucket, one packet lookahead, synchronous backpressure;
+no unbounded queue or retained output list. Input snaplen/record max 65535, at most
+2,000,000 records per replay, coverage <=24h, <=4096 quality intervals/duplicate
+declarations, manifest <=1MiB, dedup <=4096 metadata-only entries, output <=16MiB.
+Hard bounds configurable downward. Replay sink is exclusive-create, flushes every
+row, and fails closed on short write, disk full or byte ceiling. No retry, silent
+discard, overwrite or fallback counter. Source errors block COMPLETE output. A
+partial attempt file may remain for diagnosis; it is not accepted accounting.
+Unknown drops cannot be discovered from a PCAP: capture quality must be independently
+supplied. Offline capture/kernel drops = NOT_APPLICABLE, never a claimed zero.
+
+Paced load supports 19000 pps (~156.56 Mbit/s native), 38000 pps (~313.12 Mbit/s),
+1..30 seconds. It includes synthetic generation and parsing in CPU cost, samples
+current process RSS every <=190 records, tracks pacing/emission drift, queue/buffer,
+processed/rejected counts and normalized output rate. Bounded <=190-record chunks
+contain only headers. No source startup/packet consumer or production host is used.
+The test's 1-second runs are smoke checks, not sustainability evidence. Longer local
+10-second runs characterize this Windows implementation, not production coexistence
+or an official Linux PERF gate. RSS is sampled, not a hard CPU/RAM enforcement.
+
+Provisional resource-budget candidate: one pending record, <=190 replay staging
+records, one subject, one bucket; no capture queue. Any rejected input degrades,
+any structural input/output error blocks; synchronous output provides backpressure.
+Single-subject modeled storage = measured bytes per emitted slice / 5 seconds
+(86400 seconds/day). Site-wide subject cardinality and production CPU/RAM ceilings
+remain UNRESOLVED; measured Windows envelopes cannot freeze Linux systemd limits.
+
+## Runbook (offline only)
+
+From the exact candidate checkout, use the existing Python interpreter. No install:
+
+```powershell
+$env:PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX='C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-pyc'
+$python='C:\CaptivPortal-UI-Preview\.venv\Scripts\python.exe'
+& $python -m pytest tests/dti_00b -q --basetemp C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-target-01
+& $python -m compileall -q research/dti_00b tests/dti_00b
+& $python -m research.dti_00b identity
+& $python -m research.dti_00b fixture G C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-fixture-G-01
+& $python -m research.dti_00b replay C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-fixture-G-01\headers.pcap C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-fixture-G-01\coverage.json C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\tmp\dti-00b-fixture-G-01\slices.jsonl --split-visit
+& $python -m research.dti_00b reconcile --report C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\artifacts\TASK-DTI-00B-reconciliation-R1.json
+& $python -m research.dti_00b paced --pps 19000 --seconds 10 --report C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\artifacts\TASK-DTI-00B-paced-19000-R1.json
+& $python -m research.dti_00b paced --pps 38000 --seconds 10 --report C:\CaptivPortal-Lab\artifacts\TASK-DTI-00B-paced-38000-R1.json
+```
+
+Use new output/run paths per attempt; all outputs are outside Git. Stop on BLOCKED
+or nonzero exit. Do not reuse partial output or overwrite retained evidence.
+Independent reference comes from Transmission declarations before PCAP encoding,
+not parse_header/read_pcap; scenario rows retain separate expected integer totals.
+Tests also pin literal rates/bytes/half-open boundaries. A..P cover the complete
+requested synthetic scenario inventory. They do not pretend to be live-client proof.
+
+Cleanup after TechLead/Owner evidence acceptance: remove only the explicitly named
+disposable fixture directory/partial outputs through native filesystem operations;
+retain reviewed evidence according to Owner decision. No production rollback is
+needed because nothing was attached or activated. No auto-cleaner/service included.
+
+## Admission routing
+
+This package reports implementation self-check/reconciliation only. TechLead owns
+acceptance. Generic mirror provenance, Linux resource envelopes/cardinality and
+DTI01 budget remain review inputs, not fabricated PASSs. If final parser allocation
+uses production enp8s0 directly, separate Owner-authorized coexistence admission is
+mandatory (packet stealing, Fingerprint function/source health, sustained drops,
+CPU/RAM, clean detach). Offline NOT_APPLICABLE does not close that gate. DTI-01 HOLD.
+
+## R2 Linux research live adapter (r2.0)
+
+The R2 directive freezes the first placement **candidate** as an independent
+direct consumer; it does not authorize Coder to attach to any production interface.
+Coder's R2 checks use fake sockets, frames, sysfs fixtures and controlled clocks
+only. No live interface was opened during implementation/testing. Official Linux/
+production coexistence admission remains Sysadmin + Owner/TechLead responsibility.
+
+The live CLI requires explicit interface, subject MAC, capture_source_id, test
+scope, finite duration (1..300 integer seconds) and exclusive output path. There
+is no default interface or indefinite capture. Later separately authorized Lab
+operator example (NOT a command Coder executed):
+
+```sh
+python -m research.dti_00b live \
+  --interface lab0 --subject-mac 02:00:00:00:00:01 \
+  --capture-source-id controlled-linux-lab --test-scope isolated-controlled-client \
+  --duration-seconds 30 --output /absolute/disposable/new-live-slices.jsonl
+```
+
+The operator supplies an existing authorized Ethernet interface and sufficient
+CAP_NET_RAW permissions. Adapter checks Linux, Ethernet type, admin-UP and carrier
+through read-only sysfs; it does not set promiscuous mode, interface flags, BPF,
+NIC/offloads/rings, fanout/group membership or any other consumer's configuration.
+Socket creation is AF_PACKET/SOCK_RAW/protocol=0 (no reception before bind), then
+binds the supplied interface with ETH_P_ALL. No transmit path, ring, service or
+daemon installation. Nothing is imported/composed by app or run.py.
+
+It receives into one 82-byte prefix buffer using recvmsg_into + MSG_TRUNC, reuses
+parse_header, counts native IP length from corroborating original wire length,
+and zeroes the receive buffer afterwards. Only bounded parsed L2/IP metadata is
+passed onward; application payload is neither parsed nor retained. The accepted
+R1 accounting/parser/model/slice identity code is unchanged. Kernel receive
+timestamps use SO_TIMESTAMPNS_NEW when available, then OLD fallback. Missing/
+invalid/truncated timestamp metadata is explicitly degraded, never silently
+treated as exact event time. Host UTC seeds epoch-aligned 5-second boundaries;
+monotonic execution deadlines govern all waits and finite lifetime. Real-time
+clock discontinuity >250ms, receive backlog >250ms and output delay >250ms qualify
+the run; these are prototype diagnostic bounds, not final product thresholds.
+
+Timer completion occurs even with no packets. A fully covered healthy idle bucket
+can therefore be zero. Initial/final open buckets are partial. Source open/bind/
+receive/link failure yields source_unavailable, never healthy zero, with finite
+unavailable slices during the remaining requested run. Missing drop observability
+or detected kernel drops yield degraded quality. Polling is <=250ms; drop stats
+are also read before sealing. PACKET_STATISTICS counters reset on read and are
+accumulated for this socket alone. Actual SO_RCVBUF is reported (kernel may double/
+clamp requested capacity); requested <=4MiB, actual <=8MiB. Kernel queue readability
+at a seal is recorded/qualified; exact queue packet/byte depth is **not** claimed.
+No userspace packet queue, frame batch, pending slice list or live dedup cache.
+
+**NO_HEURISTIC_DEDUP / COUNT_AMBIGUOUS_OBSERVATIONS.** Live has no synthetic repeat
+map and never suppresses packet similarity. Every qualifying received observation
+counts, including repeats and retransmissions; output explicitly states
+`accounting_qualification=AMBIGUOUS_OBSERVATIONS_COUNTED_NOT_UNIQUE_TRANSMISSIONS`.
+This is the Architect-frozen qualification, not a claim of unique transmission
+counts. R1's optional trusted synthetic provenance experiment remains unchanged
+for offline compatibility; it is not a live dedup authority.
+
+Late/future event timestamps are not assigned to nearest buckets. Unassignable
+frames/native bytes and last unassigned timestamp are explicit run evidence,
+and run quality is degraded. Because already emitted slices cannot be retroactively
+rewritten, consumers must check the **whole run summary**, especially drops/late
+events/status; an earlier healthy row alone is not complete-run admission proof.
+Output errors block the attempt, never imply accepted partial JSONL. Synchronous
+backpressure is measured, not hidden or replaced by a queue. An output syscall can
+block; finite duration bounds the requested capture lifetime, not a guarantee on
+filesystem flush latency. Actual adapter stop and accounting coverage end are
+reported separately. No real-time scheduling or CPU/cgroup enforcement is claimed.
+
+SIGINT/SIGTERM request controlled stop. Finite/controlled completion obtains final
+socket statistics/queue evidence and closes the socket **before** final interval
+output. The last open interval is partial (or the more severe detected quality).
+Handlers are restored on exit; socket also closes on output/parser/resource errors.
+No future interval is fabricated after stopping; fresh runs use distinct UUIDs,
+sequence restarts, stable semantic slice IDs and existing conflict semantics.
+
+CLI prints a bounded run summary: socket open/bind/close, received/rejected/out-of-
+scope/unassigned frames, native bytes, cumulative kernel packet/drop evidence,
+receive-buffer allocation, queue-at-seal observations, timestamp mode, start/stop,
+coverage end, receive/clock/emission/output delays and quality reasons. COMPLETE
+or controlled STOPPED exits 0; DEGRADED exits 2. Exit 0 is execution status,
+**not** formal coexistence/admission PASS. Socket/output exceptions print BLOCKED.
+All existing data/output limits remain enforced. Cleanup is only the explicitly
+named disposable output after evidence acceptance; there is no installed state.
+
+R2 verification remains `pytest tests/dti_00b -q`, package compileall and diff-check
+only. No broad suite, real socket run, production action or official gate by Coder.
+
+Implementation references:
+[Linux packet socket semantics](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/packet.7.html),
+[kernel receive timestamp ABI](https://docs.kernel.org/networking/timestamping.html),
+[read-only link/carrier ABI](https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-net).
